description:
Hello! Currently the only way I've been able to validate a button is leveraging a custom `session$sendCustomMessage` to change the class of the button and the disabled properly myself, but I'd like to leverage the paradigm of the shinyvalidate pacakge in order to disable a button and display some text under it - is that possible? 

I'd like something kind of like this? (is this even possible? Any help appreciated!!

```
library(shiny)
library(shinyvalidate)

ui <- fluidPage(
   actionButton("toggle", "toggle"),
   actionButton("debug", "debug")
)

server <- function(input, output, session) {
   iv <- InputValidator$new()
   
   isTRUE <- reactive({
      (input$toggle %% 2) != 0
   })
   
   iv$add_rule("debug", function(message = "Toggle must be positive", isTRUE) {
      if (isTRUE()) { message }
   })
   
   iv$enable()
}

shinyApp(ui, server)
```

I'd like to modify the validation look and feel on the client. Following the doc example (https://rstudio.github.io/shinyvalidate/articles/displaying.html#app-level-overrides-event-handlers):

```r
library(shiny)
library(shinyvalidate)
ui <- fluidPage(
  tags$script(
    "$(function() {
      $(document).on('shinyvalidate:show', function(event) {
        console.log(event);
        let el = event.el;
        let binding = event.binding;
        let id = event.id;
        let type = event.type; 
        let message = event.message;
        event.preventDefault();
        // Add logic to show (or replace) error message on element `el`
      });
      $(document).on('shinyvalidate:clear', function(event) {
        console.log(event);
        let el = event.el;
        let binding = event.binding;
        let id = event.id;
        event.preventDefault();
        // Add logic to clear error (if one exists) from element `el`
      });
    });"
  ),
  textInput("name", "Name"),
  textInput("email", "Email")
)
server <- function(input, output, session) {
  iv <- InputValidator$new()
  iv$add_rule("name", sv_required())
  iv$add_rule("email", sv_required())
  iv$add_rule("email", sv_email())
  iv$enable()
}
shinyApp(ui, server)
```

I can see the `shinyvalidate:clear` triggering but not the `shinyvalidate:show`. 

![Screenshot 2023-03-02 at 14 16 56](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/18291543/222439720-b41c8a8a-786a-4b5a-9134-5b3a351de1d6.png)


Did I overlooked something or this is not working as expected?

Is it possible to add a method that checks if a validator is enabled or not? Something like:
```
function(self) {
  isTRUE(self$.__enclos_env__$private$enabled
} 
```
